<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec pork imports rise 76.9 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec pork imports rise 76.9 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in December rose 76.9 percent to 43,552 tonnes from 24,617 tonnes a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	 Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Total	     43,552	 31,399	 24,617</p>
<p> Refrigerated    11,605	 11,863	 11,749</p>
<p> Frozen	    31,947	 19,536	 12,868</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     5,392	  5,208	  5,181</p>
<p> U.S.		 5,366	  5,634	  5,844</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	  Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	    24,182	  12,874	 12,868</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in calendar 1996 totalled 168,859 tonnes, up 0.9 percent from 167,392 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in calendar 1996 totalled 484,274 tonnes, up 17.2 percent from 413,144 tonnes in 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
